+-C     Training Time and Hardware
+-All multi-embodiment learning experiments are conducted on AMD Ryzen 9 or AMD EPYC CPUs
+-and NVIDIA RTX 3090 or NVIDIA A5000 GPUs. For a single training run with all 16 robots and
+-the hyperparameters noted in Table 4, we allocate 20 CPU cores, 32GB of RAM and 1 GPU. With
+-this setup, training the policy for 100 million steps per robot (1.6 billion steps in total) takes around
+-2.5 days. The CPU-based MuJoCo simulation with the small amount of parallel environments (48)
+-poses the bottleneck in our training process. Moving to a more powerful GPU-based simulator with
+-thousands of parallel environments would significantly speed up the training.
