+-Figure 5 shows that using the same joint description encoder in both places leads to a slightly worse
+-performance when using the full fϕ representation and the same performance when using the partial
+-fϕ representation. Therefore, having two separate encoders for the joint descriptions does not seem
+-to be necessary. However, it might add more flexibility, allowing the policy to learn two sets of
+-encodings when needed.
