+-where σ is a learnable parameter per action dimension, and δ is a fixed scaling hyperparameter
+-(e.g., δ = 0.5). T denotes the number of timesteps within each truncated sequence (e.g., T = 20
+-during training with truncated BPTT). This loss behaves like a Huber loss with adaptive weighting,
+-allowing important joints to have higher influence during training.
+-Training is performed using batches of size 400, with truncated BPTT over recurrent states. Hid-
+-den states are detached periodically to prevent backpropagation through arbitrarily long sequences.
+-Additional details are present in Appendix C.
