+-3     Experiments
+-
+-We conduct a series of experiments to evaluate how multi-robot and multi-terrain training enables
+-generalist locomotion policies that scale across diverse quadruped embodiments and terrain types.
+-Our setup includes cross-robot training configurations with locomotion skills unevenly distributed
+-across robots. We first study zero-shot transfer and behavior fusion in stair-climbing scenarios,
+-using gait visualizations and step-wise completion tables to capture detailed behavior. We then
+-examine generalization to entirely novel terrains. Additional analyses, including comparisons with
+-and without explicit robot encodings under identical multi-robot settings, will be provided in the
+-supplementary material.
