+-3.1    Cross-Robot and Cross-Terrain Generalization Analysis
+-
+-We construct multiple training regimes using combinations of the two locomotion behaviors (pe-
+-riodic gaits and stair traversal) across different robot morphologies. Some configurations include
+-data from both flat and stair policies, while others restrict terrain or robot access to examine gener-
+-alization. Our goal is to understand how skill and morphology diversity in training data influences
+-a policy’s ability to (a) Generalize to unseen robots (cross-morphology). (b) Transfer learned skills
+-
